{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/pulls/12042","id":4997193405,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAU0OSs8AAAABKdsevQ","html_url":"https://github.com/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/pull/12042","diff_url":"https://github.com/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/pull/12042.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/pull/12042.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/issues/12042","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/pulls/12042/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/pulls/12042/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/issues/12042/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/statuses/e68e570aa1d8fbae7b4ea617751a6f1594187158","number":12042,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"redis2: pipeline entry reads when listing a directory","user":{"login":"junkerderprovinz","id":133605895,"node_id":"U_kgDOB_aqBw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/133605895?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/junkerderprovinz","html_url":"https://github.com/junkerderprovinz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/junkerderprovinz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/junkerderprovinz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/junkerderprovinz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/junkerderprovinz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/junkerderprovinz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/junkerderprovinz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/junkerderprovinz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/junkerderprovinz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/junkerderprovinz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"# What problem are we solving?\n\nSupersedes #4508 by @Woellchen, which went stale and no longer applies to the redis2 store on master. Thanks for the original idea!\n\n`ListDirectoryEntries` in the redis2 store reads every member with its own `GET`, so listing a page of 1024 entries costs 1024 round trips to Redis. When Redis sits on another host, every listing pays that latency once per entry.\n\n# How are we solving the problem?\n\nThe listing fetches the values in pipelined batches of 128, one batch each time the loop reaches it, and walks the replies in member order through the same decode step `FindEntry` uses. Every reply keeps its own error, so the loop is otherwise unchanged:\n\n- a missing value still goes through the orphaned index member cleanup and is skipped\n- a logically expired entry is still deleted and skipped\n- any other error still ends the listing at that member and is returned\n- limits, the start file name and super large directories behave as before\n\nWhy batches of 128: a full 1024 entry page takes 8 round trips instead of 1024. Some callers list with `limit` set to `math.MaxInt32` and stop after the first entry they want, for example the latest version recompute in `applyRecomputeLatest`. With one pipeline per call they would read every value in the directory; with batches they read at most 128. It also keeps any single pipeline small next to the read timeout.\n\nKept from #4508: the pipelined `GET`s from its `FindEntries`. Left out:\n\n- Writing entries with `Set(..., 0)`. That dropped the native Redis TTL, so expired values would stay in Redis until someone read or listed them.\n- The pipelined insert, update and delete paths and the renames. The listing does not need them, and their error messages wrapped the pipeline's `err` instead of the failed command's error.\n\nOn the review question in #4508 about a first batch where every entry has expired: #4508 only moved `lastFileName` on live entries, so an all expired batch came back with an empty name. Here `lastFileName` still moves past every member, as on master, and expired entries are still deleted and skipped. A page made up only of expired or missing members still returns no entries, as on master, and `ListEntries` stops there. Refilling such a page would be a separate change.\n\n# How is the PR tested?\n\nThree new tests in the gated redis2 suite:\n\n- live, missing and expired members in one page: only the live ones are listed, in order, and the rest leave the index\n- 130 entries with the member right after the first batch missing: the other 129 are listed and the index is repaired\n- a value of the wrong type: the listing stops there with an error after the entries before it\n\nThe first and third also pass on master, so the behaviour they check has not changed. The second uses the new batch size constant.\n\nRun against Redis 8.0.5:\n\n```\ncd weed\ngo build ./filer/redis2/ && go vet ./filer/redis2/\nRUN_REDIS_TESTS=1 REDIS_ADDR=<host>:6379 go test ./filer/redis2/ -count=1 -v\n```\n\nBy hand I also listed a 300 entry directory through a three node Redis Cluster, with the keys spread over all three masters and missing and expired members mixed in. The 206 live entries came back in order and the index matched.\n\nTiming at the store level (`ListDirectoryEntries` called directly, range over 7 runs) from a client to a standalone Redis on another host over the LAN, minimum PING round trip about 0.5 ms:\n\n| | master | this PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| list 1000 entries, limit 1024 | 1.3 to 1.7 s | 17 to 18 ms |\n| limit `math.MaxInt32`, callback stops after the first entry | 2.5 ms | 2.5 to 3.5 ms |\n\n# Checks\n- [x] I have added unit tests if possible.\n- [ ] I will add related wiki document changes and link to this PR after merging.\n- [ ] All AI code review comments have been addressed. No more comments to fix if reviewed again. Reviewer may request additional gemini and copilot reviews.\n\n# Checks for AI generated PRs\n- [ ] I have reviewed every line of code.\n- [x] The PR is kept as minimum as possible. Large PRs would not be accepted.\n\n<!-- devin-review-badge-begin -->\n\n---\n\n<a href=\"https://app.devin.ai/review/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/pull/12042\" target=\"_blank\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://static.devin.ai/assets/gh-devin-review-dark.svg?v=4\"><img src=\"https://static.devin.ai/assets/gh-devin-review-light.svg?v=4\" alt=\"Devin Review\"></picture></a>\n<!-- devin-review-badge-end -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Directory listings now skip missing or expired entries while preserving the order of remaining entries, and remove stale entries from the listing index.\n  * Listings spanning multiple fetch batches continue to handle missing entries correctly.\n  * If an entry cannot be read because of a Redis error, listing stops at that entry and reports the error and its name.\n\n* **Performance**\n  * Directory entries are fetched in batches, reducing individual Redis reads for larger listings.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-24T16:39:45Z","updated_at":"2026-10-24T22:04:37Z","closed_at":"2026-10-24T22:04:37Z","merged_at":"2026-10-24T22:04:37Z","merge_commit_sha":"03f773f08728790f73a8a042d66a556a07a6b908","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"junkerderprovinz:revive/4508","ref":"revive/4508","repo":null,"sha":"e68e570aa1d8fbae7b4ea617751a6f1594187158","user":{"login":"junkerderprovinz","id":133605895,"node_id":"U_kgDOB_aqBw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/133605895?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/junkerderprovinz","html_url":"https://github.com/junkerderprovinz","foll